#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kpackage; is a &GUI; interface to the <acronym>RPM</acronym>"
", Debian, Slackware and <acronym>BSD</acronym> package managers. &kpackage; is "
"part of the K Desktop Environment and, as a result, it is designed to integrate "
"with the &kde; file manager."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "Onscreen Fundamentals"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kpackage; has two panels. The left panel displays a tree of the installed and "
"available packages, the right panel displays information on the packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Main Window - Package Tree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &kpackage; is started normally (that is it has not been invoked via drag "
"and drop and has not been given any parameters) it displays two panels with the "
"package tree on the left, this tree shows installed packages and optionally new "
"and updated packages as well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Left Panel"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Left Panel - Package Tree</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Left Panel - Package Tree</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The left panel displays the list of packages, the tabs along the top determines "
"which packages are displayed:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:103
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Installed</guilabel> - Show installed packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Updated</guilabel> - Show packages for which newer versions are "
"available"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>New</guilabel> - Show uninstalled packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>All</guilabel> - All packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Below the tabs is the <guilabel>Search</guilabel> line, this filters the "
"package tree so that only those packages whose name or summary contains the "
"search string are displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The package tree is based on the sections of the distribution and shows summary "
"information about the packages:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Package</guilabel> - Name of the package"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Mark</guilabel> - Shows a tick if the package has been marked. "
"Marking allows multiple packages to be installed or uninstalled at once using "
"the buttons located below the package tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Summary</guilabel>- A short description of the package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Size</guilabel>- The package size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Version</guilabel> - The package version"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Old Version</guilabel> - If the package updates an installed package, "
"the version of the old package"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The packages have graphical labels to indicate their state, an image "
"representing the package type means an installed package, a <guilabel>"
"N</guilabel> indicates an available package and a <guilabel>U</guilabel> "
"means a package that can upgrade an installed package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A single package is selected by clicking on the name. Clicking on the dot in "
"the <guilabel>Mark</guilabel> column marks the package with a tick, a second "
"click unmarks it, while <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<mousebutton>"
"left</mousebutton></keycombo> click can be used to mark a range of packages and "
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<mousebutton>left</mousebutton></keycombo> "
"click can be used to add and remove marks on packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting a package from the tree displays information about it in the right "
"panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Main Window - Package Information Panel"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The right panel has tabs for displaying three different types of information "
"about selected packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:157 index.docbook:178 index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Right Panel - Properties"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right Panel - Package Properties"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Properties</guilabel> tab which displays information on the "
"selected package. In the dependency information there are hyper-links to the "
"packages listed, installed packages are in standard font, uninstalled but "
"available packages are in italic and dependencies that aren't available are "
"normal text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:183 index.docbook:205
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right Panel - The Files in the Package"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>File List</guilabel> tab shows the files in the package and for "
"installed packages (provided the information is available) shows the state of "
"the files. Files that exist are marked with a tick, those that are missing are "
"marked with a cross."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guilabel>Change Log</guilabel> tab shows the change log for the package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:221
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installing Packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid "To install a package you can"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"locate the package you wish to install in &konqueror;, drag it onto a running "
"copy of &kpackage;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "click on a package file in &konqueror; and start a new copy of &kpackage;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:234
#, no-c-format
msgid "use on the <guimenu>Open</guimenu> menu items in &kpackage;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "selecting an available package in the package tree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For a selected package, use the buttons in the right panel, the <guibutton>"
"Fetch</guibutton> button will fetch the package from a remote source and "
"display detailed information, the <guibutton>Install</guibutton> "
"button pops up the installation window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For marked packages, use the <guibutton>Install Marked</guibutton> "
"button on the left panel, which pops up the install window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:254 index.docbook:344 index.docbook:403 index.docbook:433 index.docbook:468 index.docbook:498 index.docbook:538 index.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Install dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Install Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Install Dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The install window lists the packages to be selected to be installed in a panel "
"in the top left, if Debain <acronym>APT</acronym> is being used the packages "
"needed to satisfy any dependencies are also shown. Below this there are a set "
"of check boxes which set options for the install program. For <acronym>"
"RPM</acronym> packages the options are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Upgrade</guibutton> - Will upgrade any already installed package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:279
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guibutton>Replace Files</guibutton> - Install the packages even if they "
"replace files from other, already installed, packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:283 index.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Check Dependencies</guibutton> - Verify dependencies."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:286 index.docbook:317 index.docbook:372 index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Test</guibutton> - Don't do the install"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:290 index.docbook:376
#, no-c-format
msgid "For Debian <acronym>APT</acronym> the options are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guibutton>Download only</guibutton> - Fetch the packages but don't install "
"them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guibutton>No download</guibutton> - Only use packages that are locally "
"available"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guibutton>Ignore missing</guibutton> - Do the install even if some packages "
"are missing"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guibutton>Ignore hold</guibutton> - Ignore holds that have been placed on "
"packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guibutton>Allow Unauthenticated</guibutton> - Ignore any requirements that the "
"packages must be signed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:313 index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guibutton>Assume yes</guibutton> - Answer yes for any questions the install "
"program would ask."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Install</guibutton> button will start the actual install. "
"Normally the install window will be deleted after a successful install but if "
"the <guibutton>Keep this window</guibutton> check box is selected the window "
"will stay around."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The panel on the right is an integrated terminal window in which the "
"installation programs are run, for interactive installation programs the "
"interaction is done in this window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "Uninstalling Packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A selected package can be uninstalled by using the <guibutton>"
"Uninstall</guibutton> button in the right panel, the <guibutton>"
"Uninstall Marked</guibutton> in the right panel can be used to uninstall marked "
"packages. The buttons bring up the uninstall window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Uninstall Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Uninstall Dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Uninstall</guibutton> button in the window causes the packages "
"to be uninstalled, and the right panel provides an integrated terminal window "
"for the uninstall program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid "For <acronym>RPM</acronym> packages the options are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Use scripts</guibutton> - Execute any unistall scripts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guibutton>Purge Config Files</guibutton> - Remove any package configuration "
"files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid "Integrating available packages in the tree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Access to available packages is setup via the <guimenu>Location</guimenu> "
"menu entries for each package type under the <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Package Handler Panel</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Package Handler Panel</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The top part of the panel has the <guilabel>Remote Host</guilabel> "
"box which allows &kpackage; to operate on the packages on a remote computer, "
"this functionality requires <command>ssh</command> and is only available when "
"using Debian apt. The name of the remote computer is entered into the combobox "
"and &kpackage; will access it when the <guilabel>Use remote host</guilabel> "
"checkbox is selected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:424
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The rest of the panel allows the enabling and disabling of the various package "
"types that &kpackage; can handle. If a package type is enabled the <guibutton>"
"Location fo Packages</guibutton> button will bring up a dialog for setting the "
"location of available packages. If the programs required for handling a package "
"type is not available the package type will be automatically disabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>RPM Location Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>RPM Location Dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For <acronym>RPM</acronym> packages &kpackage; can read a folder containing "
"packages and add these to the package tree as either new or updated packages. "
"It is possible to examine or install these packages from the package tree. By "
"default the information about the packages is extracted from the standard "
"format of the file names and so it is necessary to use the <guibutton>"
"Examine</guibutton> button to see the full description, it is possible though "
"to set an option so that for local folders each package file is read, this is "
"slower but gives a full description."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <acronym>RPM</acronym> locations dialog allows the specification of folders "
"containing <acronym>RPM</acronym> packages, it's divided up into a number of "
"tabbed panels for convenience of management. Each line in the panel specifies a "
"folder, the <guilabel>Use</guilabel> checkbox is selected the folder is used, "
"otherwise it's ignored. The text entry field can take either a folder path or "
"an <command>ftp</command> URL. The <guilabel>Subfolders</guilabel> "
"checkbox determines whether subfolders are searched for packages. The "
"<guibutton>...</guibutton> button will pop up a folder selection dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Debian Apt Location Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:476
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Debian Apt Location Dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:481
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>APT: Debian</guilabel> means that Debian packages are handled using "
"the <command>deb-apt</command> command which can automatically fetch packages "
"from repositories and resolve dependencies."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:486
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The location of uninstalled package repositories can be set in the \"A\" panel, "
"this is used to write the <filename>/etc/apt/sources.list</filename> "
"file which controls where <command>deb-apt</command> "
"searches for packages, each entry corresponds to a line in the file, if the "
"<guilabel>Use</guilabel> checkbox is not set the line is commented out."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:494
#, no-c-format
msgid "The \"D\" panel allows the specification of folders containing Debian packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:503
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Debian DPKG Location Dialog: L and P panels</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:506
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Debian DPKG Location Dialog: L and P panels</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:512
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"DPKG: Debian means that packages are handled using <command>dpkg</command> "
"command, there are three ways of accessing available packages, these can be "
"selected in three different types of location setting panels."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:518
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The \"I\" panel specifies the location of the Debian package tree and selects "
"the distribution and architecture. &kpackage; will look in the standard places "
"for the Package files describing the available packages and these packages are "
"then added to the package tree and can be examined or installed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:526
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The \"P\" panel specifies the location of the Debian distribution along with "
"the <filename>Packages</filename> files for the parts of the distribution that "
"are of interest. If the <command>dselect</command> program is being used then "
"the file <filename>/var/lib/dpkg/available</filename> "
"can be used as a <filename>Packages</filename> file that describes the "
"distribution that <command>dselect</command> uses."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:533
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The \"D\" panel specifies folders that are handled in the same way as with "
"<acronym>RPM</acronym> packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:543
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Slackware Location Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Slackware Location Dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For Slackware packages there is very little information stored on installed "
"packages, but it is possible to use a <filename>PACKAGE.TXT</filename> "
"file as a source of information about the installed packages. The <filename>"
"PACKAGES.TXT</filename> file is the equivalent of a Debian Packages file and "
"Slackware distributions are structured with a folder tree containing the "
"<literal role=\"extension\">.tgz</literal> packages and a <filename>"
"PACKAGES.TXT</filename> file that describes the packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:561
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As with Debian distributions the packages in a Slackware distribution can be "
"integrated into the package tree. Unfortunately the Slackware packages don't "
"carry version information so it is not possible to tell with available packages "
"are newer than installed ones."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:567
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The \"I\" panel is the location of a <filename>PACKAGES.TXT</filename> "
"file which is used to provided information on the installed packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:570
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The \"P\" panels can be used to specify the location of distributions with the "
"folder tree containing the <literal role=\"extension\">.tgz</literal> "
"files and the location of the corresponding <filename>PACKAGES.TXT</filename> "
"file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:574
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The \"D\" panels are for folders that do <emphasis>not</emphasis> "
"have a corresponding <filename>PACKAGES.TXT</filename> fi le"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>BSD Location Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:589
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>BSD Location Dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:594
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For <acronym>BSD</acronym> packages &kpackage; will understand a packages "
"distribution folder that contains an <filename>INDEX</filename> "
"file (which describes all the packages) and also contains an <filename>"
"All</filename> folder (with all the package files in it)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:600
#, no-c-format
msgid "The \"Ports\" panel gives the location of the ports tree in the file system"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:602
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The \"Packages\" panel allows the specifying the location of packages folders "
"&ie; those containing <filename>INDEX</filename> files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:606
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For remote folders and package files (&ie; those fetched via &FTP;) &kpackage; "
"will do caching, the packages are by default cached in <filename>"
"~/.kpackage</filename> and the folders in <filename>~/.kpackage/dir</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:611
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For the handling of remote (&FTP;) folders to work, it may be necessary to not "
"have the <guilabel>FTP Proxy</guilabel> set in the Browser Settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:618
#, no-c-format
msgid "Searching"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:620
#, no-c-format
msgid "Package Search Line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:623
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Search Line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:628
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Search Line</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:631
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Search Line</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Search line filters the package tree so that only those packages whose name "
"or summary contains the search string are displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Find Package</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:644
